     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{3}\">\\frac{2}{3}</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>For an experiment whose sample space <i>S</i> consists of equally likely outcomes, the theoretical probability of the event <i>E</i> is <span data-math=\"P(E) = \\frac{{n(E)}}{{n(S)}}\"></span>, where <i>n</i>(<i>E</i>) and <i>n</i>(<i>S</i>) denote the number of outcomes in the event and in the sample space, respectively.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"P{\\rm{(greater\\; than\\; 2)}} = P\\left( {3,4,5,{\\rm{or\\; }}6} \\right) = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}\"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
