    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>For an experiment whose sample space <i>S</i> consists of equally likely outcomes, the theoretical probability of the event <i>E</i> is <span data-math=\"P(E) = \\frac{{n(E)}}{{n(S)}}\"></span>, where <i>n</i>(<i>E</i>) and <i>n</i>(<i>S</i>) denote the number of outcomes in the event and in the sample space, respectively.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"P\\left( {odd} \\right) = P\\left( {1,3,{\\rm{or\\; 5}}} \\right) = \\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}\"></span></p>\n"
    }
